window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"darius","b":"locke","win":["Darius","Darius","Darius","Darius","Skill","Locke","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"W Crippling Strike's slow makes every trade bleed your way and follow him out of the exchange."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Full Hemorrhage stacking plus the E pull — one grab is now a genuine kill threat every wave."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Purgatory binds you inside its zone, so your Guillotine cannot leap you clear — fight before he throws it, not after."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His AP spike converts any Darius caught low — carry Grievous Wounds so Soul Ignition's refund cannot bail him out."}],"wants":{"you":["E pulls on his walk-ups","Five stacks before all-ins","Zone him off every CS"],"foe":["Poke outside pull range","Survive to first item","R conversions on a caught you"]},"early":"Ritual Nails outrange you at 950, but the marks only cash on his autos, so he has to step inside Apprehend to convert them. Level 2's W slow makes every exchange bleed your way, and 3 completes it — full Hemorrhage stacking plus the pull means one grab is a kill threat. Deny farm and make him choose between CS and health.","mid":"At 6 Purgatory binds you inside its zone, so Guillotine cannot leap you clear — and his first item is the stage to fear: AP scaling lets his R threshold and W burst convert any Darius he catches low. Commit in the ten seconds after Ashen Pursuit is spent, reset before half HP, and don't chase into fog.","late":"Two-plus items it's a standoff: whoever lands their opener — your E pull or his R execute — wins the exchange. Walk at him with five-stack Noxian Might threat, flash-pull when it kills, and in teamfights bleed everyone his totem tries to protect. Never linger at execute health; that's his entire win condition.","whys":["Darius owns level 1 — your Q heal and E pull dominate exactly the melee range he needs to poke from. He pays HP for every attempt.","Level 2 stays yours: W Crippling Strike's slow makes every trade bleed in your favor and follow him out.","Level 3 is yours outright — full Hemorrhage stacking is online and the E pull turns his poke pattern into a death sentence.","Levels 4-5 stay Darius-favored: he has no ultimate yet to answer your standing kill pressure, so keep the boot on his neck.","Level 6 evens out — Purgatory binds you in the zone so Guillotine can't leap clear, but his 120s R answers your 120s R.","First item is Locke's: AP scaling lets his R threshold and W burst convert any Darius caught low. Stay topped up and respect the totem.","Two-plus items settle even — the fight is decided by whether your E pull or his R execute lands first. Win the draw, win the game."]});
